<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Livingstone lists at 20 pct premium.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Livingstone lists at 20 pct premium.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold and diamond explorer Livingstone Resources NL made its debut on the Australian Stock Exchange on Wednesday with its shares trading at 24 cents, a 20 percent premium to the 20-cent issue price.</p>
<p>The company offered 32 million shares at 20 cents each with a free option for every two shares.</p>
<p>The company's exploration activities centre on two properties in Western Australia, one in the Golden Grove region, near Geraldton, and the other 140 km northwest of Meekatharra.</p>
<p>By 12.15 p.m. (0215 GMT), the shares had settled at 21 cents on turnover of 295,000 shares.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
